<title>USA: Niagara Mohawk finishes fish-return project.</title>
<headline>Niagara Mohawk finishes fish-return project.</headline>
<dateline>DUNKIRK, N.Y. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Niagara Mohawk Power Corp on Thursday said it completed work on a project at its Dunkirk Steam Station designed to return to Lake Erie millions of fish trapped in the facility's water-intake system.</p>
<p>The $3.25 million system enables the generating plant to comply with state and federal environmental regulations.</p>
<p>In addition to protecting the lake's fishery resources, the system will reduce landfill waste by returning to the lake valuable organic matter such as aquatic plants, the utility said.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
